## The two rules this package must keep

- **The permission check lives in the use case.** A check in a handler is a
  check the next caller — a job, a CLI command, another use case — does not
  perform.
- **The use case owns the transaction.** The store never begins one, and
  everything a single business change touches belongs inside a single `Within`
  call, so it either all happened or none of it did.
